inst hundreds  or even thousands of whites and he held  his own barrack did stand his ground and  he helped beat them back just as much as  anyone else that was standing next to  him  so obviously Barrett can still put in  some work but given his track record of  dying six times in battle forces me to  rank him low on the list now I want to  talk about grey worm and I got to be  honest again I was not very impressed  with grey worm or the unsullied at first  I knew they were an elite force but it  seemed like it took forever until we  really got to see them all in action and  grey worm has proven himself to be a  great fighter since then we have seen  his skills put on display quite a few  times now when grey worm Jorah and  Daario snuck into young Kai we get to  see just how deadly he was with his  weapon of choice then grey worm in  Barristan Selmy were outnumbered and  surrounded by the sons of the harpy grey  worm was able to kill several men with  his spear in very close quarters and  somehow he was able to survive the  attack while on the other hand Barristan  Selmy was killed  rest in peace Berenstain in season six  we get to see grey worm do this badass  move on the Masters then he led the  assault on Casterly Rock so it's pretty  obvious grey worm can hold his own just  fine but we have yet to see him fight  any actual bosses which makes it hard  for me to put him any higher let's see  how he fights in the snow against the  army of the Dead then maybe he can move  up a few notches all right so let's move  on to my next pick which is Sir Jorah  Mormont having been exiled from Westeros  from selling poachers into slavery the  night informer heir to Bear Island took  up work as a mercenary in the Free  Cities before that Jorah was said to be  at the Battle of the Trident and he  fought at the siege of Pyke during the  Greyjoy rebellion and he was knighted  afterwards by Robert Baratheon in the  television show we see Jorah kill wanna  draw goes blood riders in the very first  season we also see Jorah skills put on  display in the fighting pits Jorah has  to defend himself against several  opponents and he does survive the only  problem with Jorah is he's getting very  old and because of this he has almost  died a few times when he faces the water  dancer in the fighting pits he was  seconds away from being killed but he  was saved by the bow then when they go  beyond the wall Jorah struggles against  one of the whites thankfully Jon was  able to kill the white Walker which then  caused all of the whites to crumble but  that white was coming very close to  choking Jorah to death he can still  carry his own weight but Father time is  taking its toll on Jorah Mormont I would  like to put him higher on the list but  there are still a few people that I  think could handle Jorah pretty easily  if it came to that so let's move on to  the next one it was hard for me to put  Bronn of the Blackwater in the middle of  the list because I see him as a  jack-of-all-trades bran is experienced  with several different weapons which  makes him a very valuable asset in my  opinion bran can kill people with a  sword with a dagger and with a bow and  arrow  he's even hit drogon with the ballista  if you put any weapon in bronze hands  he's going to do damage almost  immediately after he was introduced he  was winning Tyrians trial by combat now  I know he did turn down Tyrion second  trial by combat but most men would  against the mountain on the other hand  he was ready to fight his brother the  hound  and I have to respect him for that  because that takes balls or stupidity  either way it took guts right before the  Battle of Blackwater Bay these two came  very close to fighting each other to the  death and I still wonder how this fight  would have ended I assumed the hound  would have won but at what cost  I don't think bran would have went down  very easily what I really loved about  bran is he's not afraid to get his hands  dirty and every time I see him fight he  makes it look very easy as if he's  always one step ahead of his opponent  the only thing is we haven't seen bran  get into an actual boss fight yet and I  would like to see how he stands up  against the enemies in the snow  hopefully he goes north with Jamie  because I need to see him in action  against the army of the dead now let's  talk about Arya Stark typically I would  not have her this high on the list but  based on what I've seen her do against  Brienne I had to put some respect on her  name now do I think Arya can go  toe-to-toe with bran and kill him not  necessarily but given the fact that Arya  has a particular set of skills I think  she could kill just about anyone under  different circumstances  Arya can wire different faces she can  slip behind enemy lines without being  detected and she can even kill people in  the dark she was trained not only by  Syrio Forel but also by Jack and Hegar  can you name any other character that  has had better training than Arya I  don't think so  now that she's older and a little bit  bigger combined with all of her training  this makes her very deadly  she has needle in a Valyrian steel  dagger and I think we will see her kill  at least one white Walker next season  which very few people can say they've  done what can I say about torment other  than he has been one of my favorite  characters ever since his introduction  even when he was technically on the  opposing team I could not help but love  this guy and he has proven time and time  again that he's an absolute badass I  almost had a heart attack when all of  the whites swarmed over him when they  were beyond the wall just for a few  moments I thought they were actually  gonna kill him off the show and I would  have been heartbroken then they did it  to me again when they put him on top of  the damn wall when it came crashing down  thankfully he was with the only  character that has nine lives like a cat  if anyone ever wants to question  torments fighting ability all you need  to do is watch him during the  the bastards torment has technically  been in to bossfights the first one was  against our Alliser Thorne during the  Watchers on the wall episode then he  went absolute savage again small John  umber at the Battle of the bastards I  would be confident with tormund fighting  just about anyone as long as he is  properly equipped with the right weapon  the next person I want to talk about is  Jon Snow now if this was a list where I  was ranking the greatest fighters of all  time Jon might not even be on the list  at all but when you compare him to the  current remaining characters from Game  of Thrones I think there is a case to be  made for him being one of the best  that's still alive one of the biggest  knocks against Jon is the fact that he  was nearly killed by Carl tanner who was  a fukken legend of gin alley I might add  when they fought Jon had his Valyrian  steel sword and Carl only had two small  daggers yet he was moments away from  killing Jon but John ended up being  saved just like Ned was saved  Craster's daughters stabbed him in the  back then Jon got up and finished off  the job with that being said I still  have to put Jon very high on the list  for the simple fact that he has held his  own on so many occasions Jon was cutting  through wildlings and things during the  battle for Castle black  Jon was cutting through Bolton's during  the Battle of the bastards Jon was  cutting through White's during the  mission beyond the wall and most  importantly he has killed two white  walkers they weren't lucky kills either  he went toe-to-toe blow-for-blow  and won both times which is incredible  also when and if Jon kills the night  king he will go down in history as one  of the greatest fighters of all time the  next person on the list is Gregor  Clegane who was also known as the  mountain some of you might not know this  but he was actually knighted by Rhaegar  Targaryen and in a twisted turn of  events he pays Rhaegar back by killing  his children gregor clegane is an  absolute monster he is far taller and  stronger than everyone else and he has  no morals or emotions other than rage he  has pretty much dead at this point which  means it could be tricky when trying to  kill him for good  not only that but he wears some of the  biggest armor I have ever seen and he  carries a sword that most men could not  even pick up this guy is a freak show  I would be worried if any of my  favourite characters had to face him but  I cannot put him at the top of the list  because  Martell did expose some of his  weaknesses although he ended up being  killed in the end even though the  mountain is a beast and considerably  more terrifying than most of the other  characters I think there are a few  people that could kill him in one verse  one combat he is big and strong but he  is also slow and you can Telegraph the  way he is going to swing his sword which  makes it easy to counter his strikes if  he lands one of those strikes you would  be in some serious trouble but I think  if you approached it like Oberyn did  before he let his emotions take hold of  him  I believe the mountain can be beat this  next character is easily one of my  favourite fighters on the show and that  is Brienne of Tarth  I don't think anyone can question her  skills and if they do they're just lying  to themselves Brienne is one of the very  few characters on the show that has  never lost a fight all you have to do is  look at Bryan's introduction to know  exactly what kind of character she will  be the first time we see her on-screen  is when she is beating Loras Tyrell who  was well known for winning tourneys then  she goes on to fight and beat Jaime  Lannister  now obviously his hands were tied and he  was malnourished but it was still pretty  impressive then she goes on to fight the  Hound who she nearly kills I will say at  the time the helm was not exactly a  hundred percent because of that  festering wound he received from biter  but even on the hounds worst day I don't  know too many other people that would  have been able to pull this off Brienne  is a beast and I mean that in a positive  way she even fought a damn bear I mean  come on not only that but she also  killed multiple stark soldiers at the  same time and then she kills multiple  Bolton soldiers at the same time Brienne  never backs down from a fight and  whenever she pulls out her sword you  know she is going to deliver out of all  the characters that are still alive in  this show Brienne easily falls into the  top three spot on my list without a  question the final character on the list  is Sandor Clegane also known as the  hound this man needs no introduction  his reputation speaks for itself but I  do admit I went back and forth with  where I wanted to rank him and Brienne  because she did beat him pretty bad but  I feel like I have to cut him some slack  simply because he was already nursing a  wound from a previous fight also Brienne  did have a Valyrian steel sword and if  she had a regular sword like the Hound  did  he may have cut right through just like  he did when he fought beric Dondarrion  but there is no way to prove that and  maybe Brienne would have still beaten  him even if he were healthy who knows  the hound has already had three boss  fights the first one was against his own  brother where he's shown he could hold  his own although it was cut short the  second one was against beric Dondarrion  when he cut right through his flaming  sword as if it were butter and we all  know how that ended his third boss fight  was of course against Brienne and they  both put on one hell of a show something  tells me this won't be the last time we  see the Hound faced off against a great  fighter I don't think anyone can deny  the fact that the Hound is an absolute  beast and he may be the only one that is  capable of controlling his brother in  combat which I hope we do see next  season let me know what you think which  characters would you put in your top 10  keep in mind the characters must be  alive and they can only be from the  television show I want to thank everyone  for watching this video I really  appreciate that and I also want to thank  all of you on patreon that continue to  support my channel have a great day  everyone I will see you again very soon  bye  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]
 

